@@ -0,0 +1,24 @@
+# Definition of Done
+
+> `afterModelResponse` is the hook a deployer reaches for when they need to record what a turn cost — an audit entry, a billing line, a usage budget. It is called once per user message, after the round loop exits, and is handed the `lastUsage` local: `chatOrchestrator.ts` assigns `lastUsage = outcome.usage ?? lastUsage` on each round, so what the hook receives is the usage of the final provider call alone.
+
+**Strategy: `direct`** — `createChatOrchestrator` already exposes the running `afterModelResponse` hook, so scripted provider rounds can verify its reported usage through the real tool loop. The existing single-round hook test remains the unchanged no-tool regression guard.
+
+## Done when these pass
+
+- [ ] **reports the summed usage from every provider call in a turn with two tool rounds** — `afterModelResponse` receives the total of all three provider calls made by a two-tool-round turn.
+      `src/orchestration/chatOrchestratorUsage.acceptance.test.ts`
+- [ ] **counts reported rounds while leaving a turn with no reported usage undefined** — missing round usage does not poison reported totals, while an entirely unreported turn remains undefined.
+      `src/orchestration/chatOrchestratorUsage.acceptance.test.ts`
+
+## Facets
+
+- [x] Replace final-round retention with a deliberately named total-usage contract whose public type makes aggregation explicit. (`TurnUsage` in `src/types/ai.ts`, exported from the package root; the hook parameter is `totalUsage`.)
+- [x] Sum each token field only for provider rounds that report usage, preserving `undefined` when none do. (`sumUsage` in `src/orchestration/orchestratorHelpers.ts`, wired into the round loop.)
+- [ ] Preserve the unchanged no-tool regression guard, `receives collected response text and usage`, in `src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.test.ts`. (Untouched this round; CI's verdict on the push confirms it stayed green.)
+- [x] Update the hooks spec and CHANGELOG with the aggregate-usage behavior and its impact on existing consumers. (Spec line recorded the behaviour with the acceptance link last round; the stale "issue #93 defines" clause now reads as delivered, and the CHANGELOG gained a Changed entry with a migration note.)
+- [x] Close the traceability debt CI named on 2b819a4: every test on the branch is cited by a spec statement and every citation lands on the test it names. (Repointed the four `orchestratorHelpers.test.ts` citations the `USAGE` helper's insertion moved — architecture spec; added statements citing the three `sumUsage` unit tests and the `counts reported rounds…` acceptance test; re-anchored the `chatOrchestrator.ts` `onError` gate citation 150→152, drifted by the `TurnUsage` import. `spec:names`, `check:spec-links`, `repoint-spec-anchors --check`, `docs:check`, `check:spec-status` all green here; eslint itself cannot run in this pod.)
+
+## Out of scope
+
+- Audit or billing records created by consumers, non-provider token accounting, and the provider `stop` chunk usage shape.
